# Normalise line endings in the repository, check out native.
* text=auto

# Byte-exact recordings of what raw.githubusercontent.com actually serves.
#
# `crlf_test.rs` asserts their SHA1s against a real PoB manifest, and the whole
# point of those fixtures is that the served bytes are LF while the manifest
# hash is of the CRLF-normalised form. Let git convert them on checkout and the
# recordings stop being recordings — the tests fail on every machine where
# autocrlf is on, which on Windows is the default.
tools/updater/tests/fixtures/*_lf.lua -text

# Lua the engine loads from PoB's tree is hashed by the updater; never convert.
*.lua -text

# Binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
